From 81944eb419107baa5becbba08d12bb71e7d0dbfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:50:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Blu-ray] BD-Live: Internet for the Java menus of a disc, off
 by default

A setting in the Blu-ray group of Player > Discs: bluray.hadesbdlive, "BD-Live: Internet for disc
menus", off by default (level 2). On, libbluray hands a disc with Java titles to the BD-J service
with network, which reaches IPv4 addresses of the Internet only, never this system, the home
network, other local addresses or IPv6, with names resolved by Kodi's libbluray; off, the disc has
no network at all. Its help says what it opens and what not. Spanish through Estuary (#32289,
#32290; es_es, es_ar, es_mx) and CGUIUtils::GetHadesString(), as the other settings of Hades.

kodi.log says, for each disc, whether BD-Live is on, and each name and connection of the disc's
Java, allowed or refused, without debug logging (CBlurayCallback::bluray_logger takes the lines
of libbluray with "BD-Live: " at LOGINFO). BlurayJava.h: SERVICE_HAS_NETWORK is now true, so the
line of the BD-J state says "on, to the Internet only"; its comment had a backspace character in
place of "\b" of "\brief".
